<!-- Same artwork as ic_launcher_foreground, but with a larger declared intrinsic size.
     Some platform splash-screen implementations rasterize windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon at the
     drawable's own width/height before scaling it up to the on-screen splash icon size, which
     defeats the point of using a vector if that declared size is only the standard 108dp launcher
     icon size. Bumping it well past the largest splash icon size Android ever draws (240dp) keeps
     that rasterization step, if it happens, at high enough resolution to stay sharp. -->
